+# Oncall SLO Escalation Runbook
+
+1) Alert received (PagerDuty/Slack) for SLO breach:
+ - Identify alert: SLO name, metric, instance, timeframe.
+ - Triage lead: Confirm Prometheus graph, check recent deploys (GitHub Actions logs).
+ - If false positive, annotate and suppress accordingly; if real, follow remediation steps.
+
+2) Typical remediation (webhook high error rate):
+ - Check webhook pods: kubectl -n aegis-system get pods -l app=model-provenance-webhook
+ - Inspect logs: kubectl logs -n aegis-system deploy/model-provenance-webhook -c webhook
+ - Rollback recent deployments if correlation suspected.
+ - If downstream dependency (Triton/Milvus) failing, follow their restore runbook.
+
+3) Notify stakeholders:
+ - Post incident summary to #oncall and MCP incident endpoint.
+ - If unresolved > 30 mins, escalate to oncall rotation lead and open incident in tracking system.
+
+4) Post-mortem:
+ - Collect Prometheus & Grafana dashboards, relevant pod logs, recent CI deploys and gatekeeper violations.
+ - Create post-mortem in MCP/Jira with timelines & remediation.
